This is likely at least part of the problem: 

```
  for (len(cands4) > 0 || len(cands6) > 0) && len(cands) < maxCands {
      if len(cands4) > 0 {
          cands = append(cands, cands4[0])   // IPv4 appended first
          cands4 = cands4[1:]
      }
      if len(cands6) > 0 {
          cands = append(cands, cands6[0])   // IPv6 appended second
          cands6 = cands6[1:]
      }
  }
```
This looks like it iterates through a candidate list as v4, v6, v4, v6, ... but stops at the first success, which is likely a problem for NAT64 clients. Swapping the order would probably go a long way on hosts without IPv4 even with a NAT64 or a CLAT and should force native IPv6 and then stop.

